WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.000
{IF YOU ARE SEEING THIS MESSAGE YOU ARE USING A PLAYER THAT DOES NOT RENDER THE SUBTITLES IN THIS EPISODE PROPERLY. FOR HELP GO TO: http://saizen-fansubs.com/?section=playback}

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:04.320
Excuse me!

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:06.530
You guys are part of the baseball team, right?

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.480
Y-Yes...

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:10.980
Is Shigeno-kun here?

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.710
I'd like his permission to do an interview.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.280
An interview?

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:16.250
Amazing!

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:17.590
He's famous!

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:23.800
If you're looking for Shigeno-senpai, he went with Tashiro-senpai to go check out our next opponent's game.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.260
Kuriyama against Seikai Dai Fuzoku, huh?

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:34.280
If we look at the results up till now,
then Kuriyama should be our next opponent.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.710
Whoever wins, it's the same, isn't it?

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:39.670
After one more game, we'll be able to go up against Kaido.

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:41.650
As if we could lose at a place like this.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:48.910
Those guys...

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:54.040
<i>They've gotten this much stronger!</i>

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:40.770
What is this?

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:42.380
Hey, Shigeno!

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:44.370
What's with this member list?

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:46.230
Can we really turn this in?

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.320
Shigeno went to the bathroom earlier...

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:51.200
Is there something wrong with the member list?

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:54.160
There's no what or how! Look at this...

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:56.720
Huh!?

00:02:56.720 --> 00:02:57.960
What!?

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.580
Batting first is Shigeno, and batting second is Tashiro!?

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.960
And he's the only one he wrote his full name for!

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:14.630
Oh my.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:16.840
K-Katori!

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:21.600
I wondered who it was, and it's the complete-game, no-hit shutout Goro-chan!

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:23.620
W-What the hell are you doing!?

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.570
Your bathroom's not over here!

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:27.510
Oh my.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.180
Even if I look like this, I'm a boy.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.030
Using the girl's bathroom would be bad.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:33.970
I didn't mean that.

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:36.770
The Kuriyama bathrooms are over on the first base side.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:42.440
Go over there!

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:44.790
Oh my. Being all nervous.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:47.840
Well, I guess you should be.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:49.830
If you're a man,

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:51.900
even in a game you know you'll lose, 

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:54.170
you have to get up on the mound.

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:55.990
What did you say?

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:58.800
Oh my. Did I say something that hurt your feelings?

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:02.270
Who knows that I'm losing?

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:04.500
Don't make me laugh!

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:05.740
You guys too.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:10.720
Have you forgotten that three years ago,
you lost to me at Kaido's exam?

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:15.030
Oh no, the overly confident boy.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:16.990
I'll tell you now,

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:19.950
if there'd been a second time to bat,

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:24.460
Karasawa would've definitely hit your pitch.

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.230
What?

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:31.740
Three years ago, 

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:34.300
we didn't lose to you,

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.990
we lost to Sato Toshiya. 

00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:42.440
That's right.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:47.120
We lost to Sato Toshiya and weren't able to go to Kaido.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:51.700
Even though you were able to go to Kaido because of him,

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:55.450
you're an idiot who doesn't know his place having left Kaido.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:58.150
Thanks to Toshiya... you say?

00:04:58.150 --> 00:04:59.160
Thanks to Toshiya... you say?

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:03.420
For that kind of foolish boy, 

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:06.800
we won't allow him to ever get in the way of our lives again.

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:09.000
In order to defeat that Sato,

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.170
this time for sure,

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:12.590
we'll play against Kaido.

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:16.300
How fun.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.940
Then I'll make it clear for you.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:22.720
The second chance to challenge Kaido will be mine again.

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:29.270
Why are you acting so cool when your zipper's down?

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:50.660
So that's Katori's slider, huh?

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:54.340
It definitely seems as though we won't be able to hit it at all.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:57.300
So that's why Shigeno, who practiced for this, is batting lead-off.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:58.750
Yeah.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:01.850
We have to get him up to bat as soon as possible,

00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:04.770
and make sure we don't get in his way when we're fielding.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.780
Good. I made it on time.

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:10.730
Yo, Katsuragi.

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:12.760
Yoneda-san!

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:14.240
You were here!?

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:18.450
I wanted to see the rumored Shigeno with my own eyes.

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:23.030
Top of the first inning: leading off for Seishuu High School...

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:26.910
Batting first: pitcher, Shigeno-kun.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:28.870
Play ball!

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:39.580
<i>Now then.</i>

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:43.220
<i>I guess I'll show you right from the start the results of my special training.</i>

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:48.230
Strike!

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:52.190
<i>I guess they won't be throwing sliders from the very beginning.</i>

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.850
I-It's really fast, isn't it?

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:57.190
I-It's not a big deal!

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:00.920
Strike!

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:06.660
<i>I thought that he'd come and try to hit the ball,</i>

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:10.360
<i>but he just watched low, inside, and also high.</i>

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.330
<i>Is he trying to gather information?</i>

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:16.170
Foul!

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:20.880
<i>He stepped into a fastball on the outside corner and tried to cut it?</i>

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:23.890
<i>I see. He's easy to figure out.</i>

00:07:24.470 --> 00:07:27.060
<i>The pitch he's aiming for is Katori's outpitch:</i>

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:29.940
<i>The high-speed slider on the low, outside corner.</i>

00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:32.060
All right, come!

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:34.200
Throw that slider you're so good at!

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:36.500
Show him the results of your training!

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:38.230
I wonder how that'll be.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:43.700
Even if he's practiced against an actual opponent, the speed and timing is different.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:46.430
Even if it's Shigeno-senpai,

00:07:46.430 --> 00:07:50.540
it won't be easy for him to hit it the first time he's at-bat.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:52.230
On top of that, 

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:56.040
that's <i>if</i> they haven't found out that he's aiming for the slider.

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:02.050
<i>If he's waiting for a 140km/h timing,</i>

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:03.130
<i>he won't be able to hit it.</i>

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:11.120
So he even had that kind of slow pitch!

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:12.980
So he hit it.

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:16.330
For him to hit it after his timing was messed up so badly, 

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:17.230
how smart of you.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:26.820
Out!

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:28.870
So close!

00:08:28.870 --> 00:08:30.790
Just a little bit more!

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:33.040
Damn!

00:08:35.930 --> 00:08:37.020
Could it be... 

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:38.840
the pitch he was waiting for was different?

00:08:38.840 --> 00:08:39.610
No.

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:44.430
There's no mistaking the fact that he was aiming for an outside slider and his timing was off.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:50.740
We can't take him lightly.

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:52.050
In this game...

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:57.310
it seems as though we're going to need to corner him during all of his at-bats with everything we've got.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:08:59.280
Don't mind, don't mind!

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:01.400
That was close, wasn't it?

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:03.030
This is bad.

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:06.990
They easily found out that I'm aiming for the slider.

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:11.210
During the first at-bat, I wanted to see what kinds of pitches he threw, but...

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:13.960
they didn't even let me do that.

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:17.420
This is going to be a tough game.

00:09:20.650 --> 00:09:22.380
Strike! Batter out!

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:26.470
Strike! Batter out!

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:28.520
Three outs! Change!

00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:37.230
Bottom of the first inning:
leading off for Kuriyama High School...

00:09:37.790 --> 00:09:40.940
Batting first: shortstop, Takigawa-kun.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:43.400
Yo! It's been a while.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:45.670
You're...!

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:48.450
Who're you again?

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:52.700
Hey! You forgot!? That intense battle!?

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:04.840
You're the guy from that time!

00:10:06.030 --> 00:10:08.200
So you noticed that just now?

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:09.340
That's right.

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:13.810
I’m Takigawa-sama, also known as "Takki of Hiratuska," who failed Kaido’s entrance exam because of you!

00:10:13.810 --> 00:10:15.440
Takigawa-sama.

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:19.120
I wasn't able to get into Kaido, but thanks to that,

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:23.440
I'm able to try and challenge Kaido with Karasawa and Katori.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:26.610
So just hurry up and lose.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:28.120
You.

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:29.970
Stop provoking him.

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:31.870
Oh. So sorry.

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:33.830
Play!

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:38.490
<i>Well then, once again,</i>

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:40.500
<i>I'll send you to hell!</i>

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:45.880
Strike!

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:49.730
<i>I see. </i>

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:52.770
<i>This is different from a regular fastball.</i>

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:54.380
<i>Even so...</i>

00:10:56.980 --> 00:10:57.730
He hit it!

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:03.730
What!?

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:05.210
Safe! Safe!

00:11:05.210 --> 00:11:06.280
Safe! Safe!

00:11:07.450 --> 00:11:10.700
It seems as though you've forgotten about my super speed.

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:13.370
What amazing legs...

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:16.350
For a routine grounder to the second baseman to be a hit...

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:18.450
So they'll be aiming to steal bases.

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:20.870
Of course they will.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:26.050
Batting second: left fielder, Mori-kun.

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:30.670
<i>If you can run, just try!</i>

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:31.630
Strike!

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:33.970
Safe!

00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:41.630
So he ran all of a sudden.

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:44.110
Then, of course, next should be a sacrifice bunt.

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:50.570
<i>As if I'd let you do as you please!</i>

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:53.240
Oh no!

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:54.450
Tashiro!

00:11:58.490 --> 00:11:59.510
Out!

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:01.960
All right!

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:05.000
To third, Tashiro!

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:07.320
You're too slow, idiot!

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:09.760
Oh no...

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:22.060
This is a free fansub.

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:22.060
Not for sale or rent.

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:30.070
First inning, one out, a runner on third, and the clean-up batters, huh?

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:33.530
<i>How will you get out of this sudden pinch?</i>

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:37.700
Batting third: pitcher, Katori-kun.

00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:39.870
So it's him next...

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:42.400
He's great at pitching,

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.500
but as a batter, it'll be easy, right?

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:47.280
B-But that Katori person...

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:49.210
As a batter, in this tournament, 

00:12:49.210 --> 00:12:51.460
has been credited for hitting at least half of the pitches.

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:52.640
Half!?

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:54.100
No way. Are you serious?

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:57.800
After this, the fourth batter, Karasawa-kun, is next.

00:12:57.800 --> 00:13:00.970
I would like for him to do something about it now.

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:02.250
This is pretty bad.

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:04.560
If this keeps up, they'll get a run!

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:07.610
<i>It'd be nice if it were just one run...</i>

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:15.330
<i>I don't care if it was a complete-game, no-hit shutout...</i>

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:19.160
<i>We're not so easy that you'll be able to beat us with just fastballs.</i>

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:22.620
<i>I can't give them a single run.</i>

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:24.670
<i>There's the possibility of a squeeze.</i>

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:26.080
<i>We should miss it here...</i>

00:13:26.580 --> 00:13:28.350
<i>They're not an opponent we can get so many runs off of...</i>

00:13:29.010 --> 00:13:32.000
<i>I won't allow anyone to set foot on home plate!</i>

00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:39.650
Strike!

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:41.620
All right!

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:46.050
T-Time!

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:50.470
What was up with that just now?

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:53.640
Since there's the possibility of a squeeze, I gave you the sign to waste a pitch!

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:55.860
Yeah, sorry, I wasn't watching.

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:57.150
What!?

00:13:57.150 --> 00:13:59.530
Hey, calm down, Shigeno.

00:13:59.530 --> 00:14:00.820
It's still the first inning.

00:14:01.830 --> 00:14:04.290
It's fine to give them one run.

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:06.160
Don't worry about it.

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:11.380
I'm very calm.

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:15.010
When I think I can beat them from here on,

00:14:15.010 --> 00:14:17.950
it's so much fun I started to shake with excitement.

00:14:19.110 --> 00:14:20.750
<i>That pitch just now...</i>

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:24.720
<i>It's not the fastball Takigawa hit easily.</i>

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:25.610
Play!

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.610
Strike!

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:36.050
Baseball really is something you have to watch live, Katsuragi.

00:14:37.070 --> 00:14:40.770
I understand the reason you were trying so hard.

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:44.360
Before and after a runner is in scoring position,

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:46.870
Shigeno's pitches are completely different.

00:14:46.870 --> 00:14:50.040
Especially after there's a runner on third,

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:54.840
his fighting spirit comes through clearly as he tries to not even allow a sacrifice fly.

00:14:55.300 --> 00:14:58.670
A pro can't just be talented and good at baseball.

00:14:58.670 --> 00:15:03.350
As a bad situation becomes worse, the hidden talent that comes out...

00:15:03.350 --> 00:15:05.750
What's coming out of that kid right now,

00:15:05.750 --> 00:15:08.680
is truly the aura of a professional!

00:15:11.060 --> 00:15:13.080
Strike! Batter out!

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:14.230
All right!

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:15.720
We did it!

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:16.730
Look at that!

00:15:17.300 --> 00:15:19.070
<i>That hurt!</i>

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:22.870
What's wrong?

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:25.080
I thought that you'd be able to hit at least one.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:27.420
I quit trying to hit.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:30.060
If I hurt my hand,

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:32.240
it seemed as though I wouldn't be able to pitch any good pitches.

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:33.080
What?

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:35.220
I'm joking.

00:15:35.220 --> 00:15:39.530
It's just that there wasn't a single pitch that I could hit with my bat speed.

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:41.340
But,

00:15:41.340 --> 00:15:42.750
if it's you, you'll be able to hit it.

00:15:43.660 --> 00:15:45.590
I'm counting on you, partner.

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:50.230
Batting fourth: catcher, Karasawa-kun.

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:05.530
<i>Your fastballs are easy to adjust to!</i>

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:09.540
<i>He's got it.</i>

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:14.630
Foul!

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:18.300
<i>So it hit the top...</i>

00:16:18.300 --> 00:16:20.550
<i>But that's enough.</i>

00:16:20.550 --> 00:16:24.300
<i>I've already outclassed the location of your pitches.</i>

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:27.820
As expected of Karasawa... His timing is perfect!

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:30.300
Blast a fly into the right field stands next time!

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:41.110
Man. What is he doing?

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:43.730
<i>I swung too late!? There's no way!</i>

00:16:44.530 --> 00:16:48.240
<i>I should've adjusted my timing and location!</i>

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:50.040
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:51.990
<i>So sorry...</i>

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:53.710
<i>The pitches I throw... </i>

00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:57.460
<i>Unlike a machine, every pitch is different!</i>

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:05.930
Strike! Batter out!

00:17:07.010 --> 00:17:08.550
We did it!

00:17:08.550 --> 00:17:09.930
Nice ball, Shigeno!

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:12.430
First pitch, 150km/h.

00:17:12.430 --> 00:17:14.850
Second pitch, 153km/h.

00:17:15.520 --> 00:17:18.440
And the one right now was 156km/h.

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:22.130
So this is his ability as of now.

00:17:22.130 --> 00:17:25.860
It seems as though he hasn't changed at all.

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:42.670
Still no runs and it's the seventh inning, huh?

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:45.880
It's completely a pitchers' duel, isn't it?

00:17:45.880 --> 00:17:47.720
That's not all.

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:51.540
We still have no hits and not even a walk.

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:52.720
So?

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:57.360
At this rate, they're going to have a perfect game.

00:17:58.190 --> 00:18:02.400
Even so, we can't get them at all.

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:05.860
We can only have Shigeno do something for us!

00:18:09.070 --> 00:18:10.320
Strike!

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:13.500
<i>You're still waiting for a slider?</i>

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:15.740
<i>No matter how long you wait, you're not going to get it.</i>

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:19.050
Strike!

00:18:20.650 --> 00:18:22.920
They've easily put us in trouble again!

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:25.700
<i>It's the seventh inning already, Shigeno!</i>

00:18:25.700 --> 00:18:30.050
<i>Even though you practiced, you can't wait and hit a pitch that will never come.</i>

00:18:30.050 --> 00:18:33.890
<i>Now then, let's take our time and destroy you!</i>

00:18:37.210 --> 00:18:38.180
Ball!

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:42.750
<i>You watched it carefully. </i>

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:45.860
<i>However, if you care so much about the outside,</i>

00:18:45.860 --> 00:18:48.240
<i>you'll miss the shootball inside!</i>

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:50.780
Foul!

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:53.500
You escaped it well.

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:55.490
Of course.

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:57.660
These kinds of B-rank breaking balls...

00:18:57.660 --> 00:19:00.100
I already saw them during my second time at bat.

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:02.360
The shoot, curve, and change-up...

00:19:02.360 --> 00:19:06.380
In the end, it's not his outpitch, right?

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:12.430
Now you've said it!

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:13.680
Foul!

00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:14.680
Foul!

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:16.100
Foul!

00:19:17.230 --> 00:19:18.060
Ball.

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:20.100
Ball.

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:26.570
<i>Calm down, Katori.</i>

00:19:26.570 --> 00:19:30.030
He stuck with it and got the count to 3-2, huh?

00:19:30.030 --> 00:19:32.540
What's taking him so long?

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:35.370
No one likes persistent guys like you!

00:19:39.660 --> 00:19:41.120
Foul!

00:19:42.310 --> 00:19:43.330
So close!

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:52.090
He's finally got them cornered.

00:19:52.930 --> 00:19:53.680
What?

00:19:53.680 --> 00:19:57.790
In the end, senpai finally cornered that battery.

00:19:57.790 --> 00:20:02.140
They can only throw a slider now.

00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:05.000
<i>It was a fastball low and outside.</i>

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:07.610
<i>I don't care if we walk him!</i>

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:13.610
<i>Let me throw it, Karasawa.</i>

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:20.330
<i>My high-speed slider isn't a pitch you can aim for and still hit.</i>

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:22.170
<i>Karasawa.</i>

00:20:22.170 --> 00:20:23.560
<i>Trust my... My slider!</i>

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:25.490
<i>Trust my... My slider!</i>

00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:34.380
<i>It's coming!</i>

00:20:35.860 --> 00:20:37.470
<i>I've been waiting for this!</i>

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:51.240
Strike! Batter out!

00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:56.360
Damn it!

00:20:57.150 --> 00:21:01.440
It seems as though they were making being able to hit that slider the point of the game,

00:21:01.950 --> 00:21:04.630
but he wasn't able to hit it that easily after all...

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:06.670
I hope he doesn't snap.

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:12.090
In these last innings, where your heart and body start to get tired,

00:21:12.090 --> 00:21:15.280
and the reality of your own team having no chance of winning starts to set in...

00:21:15.280 --> 00:21:18.050
There's nothing that can make a pitcher more depressed.

00:21:18.050 --> 00:21:19.860
The next inning,

00:21:19.860 --> 00:21:24.020
where he'll be going up against the third and fourth batters, will be the hardest part for Shigeno.

00:21:25.510 --> 00:21:27.280
Strike! Batter out!

00:21:27.280 --> 00:21:28.910
Three outs! Change!

00:21:30.230 --> 00:21:31.920
Again...

00:21:31.920 --> 00:21:35.700
At this rate, they'll really get a perfect game!

00:21:35.700 --> 00:21:37.740
<i>This is the worst.</i>

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:39.600
<i>It's an amazing pitch.</i>

00:21:39.600 --> 00:21:42.160
<i>I knew it was coming, yet I couldn't hit it.</i>

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:48.820
<i>So it means that this guy's slider wasn't something you could hit with just a bit of practice.</i>

00:21:50.190 --> 00:21:51.700
<i>Even... </i>

00:21:51.700 --> 00:21:54.460
<i>Even if we're able to hold these guys back the next few innings,</i>

00:21:54.460 --> 00:21:56.590
<i>will we be able to score any runs?</i>

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:06.810
Batting fourth: catcher, Karasawa-kun.

00:22:12.070 --> 00:22:15.530
<i>Katori, who couldn't hit it at all before, is able to hit it now?</i>

00:22:15.530 --> 00:22:19.030
<i>This guy... isn't my rival!</i>

00:22:19.500 --> 00:22:21.030
<i>Do your best, Shigeno.</i>

00:22:21.030 --> 00:22:24.950
<i>Just win one more game, and it's the Kaido game that you've dreamt about!</i>

00:22:35.510 --> 00:22:37.920
<i>The ones to go up against Kaido...</i>

00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:39.380
<i>will be us!</i>

00:22:58.750 --> 00:22:59.860
Shigeno!

00:23:00.330 --> 00:23:02.350
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:23:02.350 --> 00:23:05.370
<i>The painkillers are starting to wear off...</i>

00:24:39.880 --> 00:24:42.580
Going into the last inning with them having a two-run lead...

00:24:42.580 --> 00:24:47.350
Seishuu is counting on our pinch hitter, Taiga, and his bat!

00:24:47.350 --> 00:24:48.790
Just you wait, Kaido.

00:24:48.790 --> 00:24:51.680
I'll definitely turn this around and challenge you!

00:24:52.160 --> 00:24:53.510
Next time, on Major:

00:24:53.510 --> 00:24:54.900
Last Spurt!

00:24:54.900 --> 00:24:57.580
Run to the stage of your dreams!
